    "body": "Closes #40641\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\nno way to work with (reorder, filter, etc.) dir.lua ordering\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nexpose a user `NvimDirRender` that the end user can document to do so, temporarily marking the buffer as modifiable during the change. the user is responsible for creating invalid state through the autocmd.\r\n\r\n@jfly",
    "closed_at": null,
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "\r\n\r\nwhy can't the user just handle `FileType directory` , why is a new event needed? \r\n\r\n> temporarily marking the buffer as modifiable during the change\r\n\r\nif we really don't want to make the buffer always 'modifiable' (why?), we can just show an example in the user handler which includes `:set modifiable`",
            "created_at": "2026-08-04T08:55:36Z",
